        "id": "640134c64567e1fa2ea931c88c5854627bb4b623",
        "tree_id": "c06588ea15e6d209475113a2a4f80703363d98bb",
        "message": "docs: ISSUE-LOG — 14/14, and a real product bug the switch did not gate\n\nRun 36707513732, x86_64 emulator. Fourteen tests, no failures, no skips.\n\nA REAL PRODUCT BUG, FOUND BY WRITING THE TEST THAT SHOULD HAVE EXISTED.\n\nChatRepository.streamLocalReply is the path taken when the PROVIDER FAILS, and\nit read\n\n    val reply = nativeReply(prompt) ?: localReply(prompt)\n\nunconditionally. nativeReply() calls GsNative.chat. So with \"Prefer on-device AI\"\nOFF -- the default, and the setting a user turns off precisely to stop prompts\nreaching an on-device model -- an unavailable network was enough to send the\nprompt there anyway. That is the opposite of the property the switch exists for,\nas commit 1(b) states in the same file.\n\nNow gated on SettingsStore.preferLocal. The canned responder is NOT removed: a\nphone with no model, a build with no engine, or a generation that throws must\nstill answer.\n\nTWELVE GREEN TESTS NEVER CAUGHT IT. a1 and a6 run with the engine available and\nneither reaches streamLocalReply; a6 exercises streamLocalFirst, the local-FIRST\nbranch, which was correctly gated. The provider-FAILED branch had no test.\n\nProven on a real device by a7:\n\n    LocalFirstToggleTest: OFF -> — GS backend error (HTTP 0) —\n    LocalFirstToggleTest: ON  -> Paris.\n\nThe two branches DIFFER, which is what makes it a routing test -- two independent\nassertions pass whether the flag is wired up, inverted, or ignored entirely.\n\nAND THE NEW TEST THAT WAS ITSELF A FALSE PASS\n\na8 pointed ApiClient at 127.0.0.1:1, which yields SendFailure.BackendError, and\nthat arm of send() RETURNS at that line without ever calling streamLocalReply. So\na8 never invoked the canned responder once, and \"reply is not blank\" was\nsatisfied by the error marker. Run 36707513732 printed the identical string for\na8 and for a7's OFF branch, which is what exposed it.\n\na8 now serves a real chunked SSE response from a raw ServerSocket and hangs up\nmid-stream -- the case localReply() exists for -- and asserts the responder's\ntext is present and the marker is not. No new dependency: build.gradle.kts has\nonly the ktor client artifacts, and adding a server to the app for one test is\nthe wrong trade.\n\nTwo more entries recorded:\n\n    24  libggml-metal.a references Metal/ObjC symbols that the CARGO link cannot\n        resolve, because cc is the linker driver and project.yml's OTHER_LDFLAGS\n        only reaches xcodebuild. Both links need the frameworks, from different\n        files.\n    25  a8 asserted on the backend-error marker, which returns before\n        streamLocalReply is ever called.",
